{{! Uniform "claim unavailable" page.

    Rendered when a claim against a historical-person record cannot proceed
    for any reason: the record does not exist, has already been claimed, is
    already linked to a legacy account, the surname on the record does not
    match the requesting account, the requesting account is linked to an
    incompatible legacy record, or any other validation failure. The page
    intentionally does NOT distinguish between these cases: all failure
    reasons map to the same response so the page cannot confirm which
    person IDs exist (anti-enumeration). The operator can resolve the
    specific cause from the application log written at render time.

    Because it is uniform, the copy has to be true and useful for every one
    of those reasons. It leads with the two self-serve remedies, which are
    the ones that resolve the commonest cause, a name that does not line up,
    and which give the reader something to do rather than someone to write to.

    Everyone who reaches this page is still a registrant: both claim entry
    points send a member who has finished onboarding to the admin request form
    before any lookup runs. So the page offers no administrator link, which
    would be a member capability this audience cannot reach, and says instead
    when that route becomes available to them.
}}

<div class="hero hero-sm">
  <div>
    <h1>{{page.title}}</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrapper">
  <section>
    <p>We could not link this record to your account.</p>

    <p>If you used a different surname before, or a different email address on the old footbag.org, add either one in the claim step and we will look again. Your date of birth helps too, so it is worth checking that it is right.</p>

    <p class="mt-4"><a href="{{content.claimStepHref}}" class="btn btn-primary">Add a Former Name or Old Email</a></p>

    <p class="mt-6">If you have tried that and this is still your record, an IFPA administrator can link it for you once you have finished signing up.</p>

    <p class="mt-6"><a href="{{content.cancelHref}}">Back to the record</a></p>
  </section>
</div>
